# Recovery from scripted disk images, each on a freshly formatted 1 GiB disk (64-block segments,
# segment 1 the hot stream's from block 64, segment 2 the cold stream's from block 128).
# run [depth=n] [plant=stop-early|past-gaps] takes commands, one per line; a plant breaks every
# recovery the case runs, as disklog.StopEarly or disklog.ReplayPastGaps does:
#   write <hot|cold> <chunk> <first> <count> <version>   a chunk write, submitted and completed
#   submit <hot|cold> <chunk> <first> <count> <version>  submitted only; prints the actions it queues
#   exec ioN                                              executes pending action ioN
#   crash [lba...]                                        crashes, landing only these unflushed blocks
#   xor <lba> <mask>                                      XORs every byte of a block with mask
#   flip <lba> <byte> <mask>                              XORs one byte of a block with mask
#   zeros <lba>                                           whether a block reads as zeros
#   recover <open|rebuild>                                recovers and prints the LSNs replayed
#   index                                                 prints the last recovery's index, each
#                                                         extent's chunk, blocks, version, pool and
#                                                         LBAs, whether every block reads back, and
#                                                         whether it is what the crash oracle holds
#                                                         at the recovered LSN: every acknowledged
#                                                         record and the written ones up to it
# go test -rewrite regenerates the output.

# Torn tail (RocksDB TruncatedTrailingRecord, PartialLast): three 2-block writes, then a fourth
# round written but not flushed. A crash landing none of its blocks recovers LSNs 1-3.
run
write hot 0 0 2 1
write hot 1 0 2 2
write hot 2 0 2 3
submit hot 3 0 2 4
exec io110
crash
recover open
index
----
submit hot 3 0 2 4: write 74+3 io110, fsync io111
recover open: LSNs 1-3, durable 3
index: 6 blocks, every block reads back, as the oracle expects at LSN 3
  chunk 0 blocks 0-1 v1 pool 1 at 66-67
  chunk 1 blocks 0-1 v2 pool 1 at 69-70
  chunk 2 blocks 0-1 v3 pool 1 at 72-73

