# Damage in a middle record is corruption, not truncation, and open and rebuild agree: record 2's
# header XORed with 0x5A (RocksDB ErrorJoinsRecords), and one flipped bit in record 3's header or
# data, or in record 4's header, the last but one, of 5 records (PAR, FAST 2018).
run
write hot 0 0 2 1
write hot 1 0 2 2
write hot 2 0 2 3
write hot 3 0 2 4
write hot 4 0 2 5
xor 68 0x5a
recover open
recover rebuild
----
recover open: Corrupt(LSN 2)
recover rebuild: Corrupt(LSN 2)

run
write hot 0 0 2 1
write hot 1 0 2 2
write hot 2 0 2 3
write hot 3 0 2 4
write hot 4 0 2 5
flip 71 60 1
recover open
recover rebuild
