# Damage in the last record's data cannot be told from a torn write, so it recovers as a crash,
# and the oracle names the acknowledged record it lost; it then takes the recovered index as its
# model, so a later write recovers as the oracle expects.
run
write hot 0 0 2 1
write hot 1 0 2 2
write hot 2 0 2 3
write hot 3 0 2 4
write hot 4 0 2 5
flip 78 7 4
recover open
index
write hot 5 0 1 6
recover open
index
